{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle","id":1045709,"title":"Playing a Sorcerer in a Mage Chronicle?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-08T06:22:40-08:00","id":1045709,"title":"Playing a Sorcerer in a Mage Chronicle?","content":"So the Technocracy, Traditions and Disparates all have Sorcerers working for them as Specialists, in some number or form. The Technocracy is mostly Unawakened Extraordinary Citizens, and among those (if the ST is using Sorcerers) there are many Sorcerers. So, it's not impossible that a group of Mages could be assigned a Specialist Sorcerer to assist them in some regard they excel in (transport, requisition, combat, exploration).<br /> <br /> Here are the two major questions: (1) Would you allow a PC to play a Sorcerer? What sort of games/settings would they suit? (2) If you did include a Sorcerer PC, how would you run Character Creation? Equal For All is an obvious choice, but Mages get 6 dots in Spheres and Sorcerers get 5 dots in Paths. What balancing factors would you include?<br /> <br /> (1) From what I can see, this would be best suited to a Chronicle where the Players have a certain defined goal (at least at the beginning) or unifying cause, which could allow for a certain role to be filled by a Specialist. An example might include a Scouting party into an area controlled by another group, unraveling a Technocracy/Tradition plot, dealing with some Night-Folk menace, attempting to fulfill some goal on the way to Mass Ascension. Alternatively, you have a tabletop Classic; the prison-break scenario. The PCs all begin captured by the Technocracy in a mid-sized base, all having been detected, betrayed or outsmarted. This allows for a mix of Traditions, Disparates (even Orphans) and potentially a Sorcerer. This assumes your Technocracy doesn't Kill On Sight and at least attempts conversion or study. The group break out together and this leads to the discovery of Story Threads which take them towards the Plot at large. Obviously there are notable benefits to a group including a Sorcerer, since they can ignore Paradox and Reality Zones, have good Counter-magic and are precisely limited in what they can do (potent but static) making them less prone to unexpected and frightening effects. Since they don't need to deal with The Quiet or the other downsides of being Awakened, they can more easily keep an eye on their comrades' mental health and sanity.<br /> <br /> (2) There are some options here. Your Sorcerer could simply be given extra Freebie points, 10 starting dots in Paths, extra Backgrounds... or they could be given some alternative source of power. Perhaps they're a Lost Revenant, giving them healing powers, blood pump, ability to soak Lethal and 2 dots in Disciplines. Revenants are sources of Quintessence roughly akin to a weak Vampire (20 I believe), making them potent Apprentices and Allies. You could simply give the Sorcerer a head-start on EXP; run character generation and then give them the EXP of someone who has been studying for 10 years rather than 5 and apply it to the sheet.<br /> <br /> How do you all address (1) and (2)? Does anyone have any experience with this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T06:34:00-08:00","id":1045712,"title":"","content":"Why do they need anything extra? Most Mage aren't self healing nor do they soak lethal without armor, especially at the start. Why would a Sorcerer need this? You just had a thread where you talked about how bad@$$ Sorcerers are now you feel they needed a boost for inclusion in a Mage Story?<br /> <br /> Sorcerers are fine in Mage games as they are. As I mentioned in the other thread all that is a bit out of wack is countermagic and even that is only do to all splats using 2 sourcers for a dice pool (mostly) where as the Mage get only 1 for Arete. Though most successes count as good as 2 ( for damage at least) that requiring double successes to counter them with non True Magick countering effects isn't out of line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":".  Hit post by accident before done. 02-08-2017, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T06:38:26-08:00","id":1045715,"title":"","content":"I would either run a Mage game, or a Sorcerer game. Having a mixture of players is certainly possible, but it's a hell of a lot more to keep track off, especially in regards to who counts as a witness for which mage when doing vulgar magic.<br /> That's a headache I'm not quite ready to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T06:47:12-08:00","id":1045720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1045712#post1045712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do they need anything extra? Most Mage aren't self healing nor do they soak lethal without armor, especially at the start. Why would a Sorcerer need this? You just had a thread where you talked about how bad@$$ Sorcerers are now you feel they needed a boost for inclusion in a Mage Story?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was saying, quite simply (in a thread I didn't start, I contributed to) that Sorcerers <i>can</i> be &quot;badass&quot; in very limited spheres of life which they devote a tonne of time and energy to. A Character built from the ground up to be the perfect manufacturer is going to trump Mages of similar experience in that very very limited aspect of existence... while the Generalist Mage trumps them in everything else. If you were to torture the meaning of my words you might be able to come out with that impression, so whatever. And no, Mages aren't self-healing and don't soak Lethal, but at the same time Sorcerers aren't Spherical and can't make shit up on the fly. Obviously you can't balance Sorcerers by making them Spherical since that would just make them Mages, so you need to give them something Mages don't have. That's what balance <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> Mages can combine, reframe, invert and balance their powers as they wish, within the scope of their Paradigm. While the Sorcerer Masters healing, a Mage with Life learns not just to heal, but also to transform, grow and fundamentally alter life. It would be idiotic to say that Sorcerers when compared to Mages are generally superior, they are very very specifically superior if they are devoted to one field of study.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, just reading the books, Sorcerers are touted by the Sorcerer books as being good for non-Mage games since Mages simply can't be compared to other Splats mechanically. The books make it patently clear that a starting Mage trumps a starting Sorcerer overall, and it's only when a Sorcerer is built for a purpose (transport, combat, espionage, logistical support) that they can really shine. When thrown into a coterie of Awakened Mages, I think it's fair that the precisely limited Player Character be given some boost for the purpose of fun, which is what this is all about. If they're infinitely weaker that won't be fun, the majority of the time, as they become a dead weight holding the group down.<br /> <br /> Also, dude, that's just threadcapping. At least tell me why you think Sorcerers don't need bonuses at start, rather than just saying they don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T06:50:04-08:00","id":1045723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1045715#post1045715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would either run a Mage game, or a Sorcerer game. Having a mixture of players is certainly possible, but it's a hell of a lot more to keep track off, especially in regards to who counts as a witness for which mage when doing vulgar magic.<br /> That's a headache I'm not quite ready to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerers count as Sleepers in only two situations. One, we have Techno-Sorcerers, who have been conditioned by the Technocracy to believe that reality deviance is impossible. They'll count as Sleeper Witnesses for all Mages who are non-Techno. Secondly, we have Sorcerers who come from a place where they have never ever seen Technology. Here they also count as Sleeper Witnesses for Technological Magick.<br /> <br /> Those two situations are simply dealt with. Either make your Technocratic Technosorcerer part of a Technocracy game (don't want them stopping the Mystics from having fun), which would make them a potent ally as they would be an effective weapon against Antagonist Mages, or you make them play as a type of Sorcerer who will never count as a Sleeper for anything (the vast majority of Sorcerers, including all but a few Mystics and quite a lot of Scientifics).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T06:50:11-08:00","id":1045724,"title":"","content":"Saikou mildly brings up a great point. One I have for crossovers in general though a Sorcerer/Mage crossover is less problematic than most. Crossover characters work best under the STs controll, otherwise their are alwaya headaches involved. Many of which you don't immediately see comming. Of course many people play crossovers all the time but the amount of work by the ST is much more involed than a game without.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T06:56:25-08:00","id":1045730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1045723#post1045723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorcerers count as Sleepers in only two situations. One, we have Techno-Sorcerers, who have been conditioned by the Technocracy to believe that reality deviance is impossible. They'll count as Sleeper Witnesses for all Mages who are non-Techno. Secondly, we have Sorcerers who come from a place where they have never ever seen Technology. Here they also count as Sleeper Witnesses for Technological Magick.<br /> <br /> Those two situations are simply dealt with. Either make your Technocratic Technosorcerer part of a Technocracy game (don't want them stopping the Mystics from having fun), which would make them a potent ally as they would be an effective weapon against Antagonist Mages, or you make them play as a type of Sorcerer who will never count as a Sleeper for anything (the vast majority of Sorcerers, including all but a few Mystics and quite a lot of Scientifics).</div> </div> </div> </div>And what about sorcerers with True Faith, with Psychic Numina, with Qi energy powers? If you're going to lump them all in the &quot;mystic&quot; bin, then what's the point in defining them at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 02-08-2017, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:05:44-08:00","id":1045734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1045730#post1045730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what about sorcerers with True Faith, with Psychic Numina, with Qi energy powers? If you're going to lump them all in the &quot;mystic&quot; bin, then what's the point in defining them at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not lumping them in the Mystic bin, the rules are. If you can move stuff with your mind, and you see a person moving something with a staff with runes, you will think &quot;huh, they're a psychic with this weird magical fetish&quot;. If you have True Faith and you see someone summoning up spirits, you'll think &quot;the adversary has granted this person power&quot; or &quot;My Father's House Has Many Rooms&quot; or &quot;is this some other form of Faith?&quot;. If you think that your clearly supernatural Karate (which can do superhuman things) is fueled by Qi, and you witness someone breathing fire, you'll think &quot;CAN I DO THAT?!?!&quot;. Also, I'm not personally a big fan of psychics, I don't consider them &quot;Sorcerers&quot;, but I'm glad they were in the book.<br /> <br /> In the case of True Faith, if they have True Faith and nothing else, and have never used it for supernatural purposes or encountered the supernatural, they would count as a Sleeper, but that's not what we're talking about. We're assuming the ST has the sense to only include a Nun with True Faith who assists the Celestial Choir if they are open to the concept of Magic existing, since otherwise this agent would be actively hampering the Traditions. STs can exercise some good judgement here.<br /> <br /> The only reason that purely Technologically enlightened Sorcerers can't accept magic is that their paradigm is so restrictive that it simply can't explain &quot;breathing fire&quot; ever. The Hermetic can see 1000 people breathing fire in 1000 ways and identify his method as the REAL reason they're able to do it. That doesn't work the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-08-2017, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:19:59-08:00","id":1045742,"title":"","content":"If I was running a mage game, I'd probably caution players if they wanted to play a Sorcerer. I don't really see any appeal to playing a sorcerer when you could play a mage in an explicitly mage game. And to that extent, I probably wouldn't go out of my way to give them anything special for character creation beyond what a mage is being giving for creation. I guess I would see it as if someone wanted to play a kinfolk or ghoul. If that's what you want and enjoy, seems fine. The emphasis is going to be (hopeful) on character. I guess I don't see a need to balance the sorcerer to the mages if they are intentionally choosing to play a weaker mini-splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:22:41-08:00","id":1045744,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a> Would the same rules work on these sorcerers being able to use wonders? Because the way that Artefacts have worked historically is that only sleepers (sorcerer or not) who believe in the principles behind their inception would be able to use them. You can only use your fairy wings to fly if you believe they have fairy powers (ignoring changeling stuff for the moment.) You can transform water into wine with a special chalice because you're a devout christian. You can only use a magic wand because you're so certain all this occult stuff is real. You can fiddle with a Lightning Gun because &quot;I've seen these work at expos!!&quot;.<br /> <br /> However, if they are all functionally the same where they won't count as witnesses, then a Qi energy sorcerer should have no problem wielding a wand.<br /> <br /> Conceptually, I have a problem with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:26:50-08:00","id":1045745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1045742#post1045742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was running a mage game, I'd probably caution players if they wanted to play a Sorcerer. I don't really see any appeal to playing a sorcerer when you could play a mage in an explicitly mage game. And to that extent, I probably wouldn't go out of my way to give them anything special for character creation beyond what a mage is being giving for creation. I guess I would see it as if someone wanted to play a kinfolk or ghoul. If that's what you want and enjoy, seems fine. The emphasis is going to be (hopeful) on character. I guess I don't see a need to balance the sorcerer to the mages if they are intentionally choosing to play a weaker mini-splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you allow freebie points from Flaws? Why do you feel a need to balance characters who intentionally choose to play someone with a limp or mental illness?<br /> <br /> And I agree, there should be an emphasis on character! The implication that wanting mechanical recompense for playing as a mini-Splat somehow goes against RP or organic characters is The Stormwind Fallacy, however.<br /> <br /> I agree that Ghouls and Kinfolk can be fun with no balancing whatsoever, and I've seen them both work well. However, those are differences of degrees, not kind. The Kinfolk have weaker gifts and a single form, the Ghouls have weaker Disciplines and a lesser status. Mages, on the other hand, are not just Sorcerers who start with higher levels in Paths, they don't use Paths at all. Kind, not Degrees. Now playing a Sorcerer with no balancing whatsoever certainly could be fun, however if an ST decided that they did want to balance it, what would you recommend? That was basically my initial request, ideas on balancing the two types of Starting Character at least a little bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-08-2017, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:27:56-08:00","id":1045746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1045744#post1045744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a> Would the same rules work on these sorcerers being able to use wonders? Because the way that Artefacts have worked historically is that only sleepers (sorcerer or not) who believe in the principles behind their inception would be able to use them. You can only use your fairy wings to fly if you believe they have fairy powers (ignoring changeling stuff for the moment.) You can transform water into wine with a special chalice because you're a devout christian. You can only use a magic wand because you're so certain all this occult stuff is real. You can fiddle with a Lightning Gun because &quot;I've seen these work at expos!!&quot;.<br /> <br /> However, if they are all functionally the same where they won't count as witnesses, then a Qi energy sorcerer should have no problem wielding a wand.<br /> <br /> Conceptually, I have a problem with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well isn't that a whole other issue? So our Ki-user isn't a &quot;Witness&quot; when he sees someone using a wand (&quot;ah, that stick must allow them to focus their Ki! Unfortunately the fool doesn't understand that the body is the best tool for focusing Ki, even if he is mighty&quot;), however that doesn't mean you can just hand it to him and he can use it. Two separate issues.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, with very few exceptions, Sorcerers count as Night-Folk and are not Sleepers, since they see the supernatural on a daily basis (see M20). HOWEVER they can count as Sleepers in very, very rare circumstances, such as when they have the Sleeper Merit (an optional merit in the optional merits system which the ST can simply disallow, as they would ruin ALL of the Magick) or have a backstory which makes them a Sleeper for non-tech or for tech (something you can disallow if it would get in the way of the Magick).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-08-2017, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:33:00-08:00","id":1045749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1045746#post1045746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well isn't that a whole other issue? So our Ki-user isn't a &quot;Witness&quot; when he sees someone using a wand (&quot;ah, that stick must allow them to focus their Ki! Unfortunately the fool doesn't understand that the body is the best tool for focusing Ki, even if he is mighty&quot;), however that doesn't mean you can just hand it to him and he can use it. Two separate issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? That's how Wonder's work, you can only use them if you believe they will work. If you don't believe it could work, and your avatar isn't awakened, you're a sleeper witness. Otherwise they'd be an acolyte.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:36:57-08:00","id":1045752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1045749#post1045749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? That's how Wonder's work, you can only use them if you believe they will work. If you don't believe it could work, and your avatar isn't awakened, you're a sleeper witness. Otherwise they'd be an acolyte.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this specific case, you can say that they believe it works, but simply isn't for them. The Ki-user sees the wand as something apart from them, but doesn't doubt that it works since it's no more weird than him punching something and it crackling with electricity/flames/light. He'll see it in his terms, pouring your Ki into an object, but he won't assume he knows how to use the object or that it will work for him.<br /> <br /> If Wonders are &quot;if you believe in this it will always work&quot;, then that's a slightly un-nuanced approach. Surely it would make more sense within the wider scope of Paradigms and the Mage Lore if Wonders only worked if you believe that they will work for you? Why does the non-sleeper who uses a wand suddenly think that a set of magical wings will work for him on the first try? They can doubt that they can use them and still not be a sleeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:00:49-08:00","id":1045757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1045752#post1045752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this specific case, you can say that they believe it works, but simply isn't for them. The Ki-user sees the wand as something apart from them, but doesn't doubt that it works since it's no more weird than him punching something and it crackling with electricity/flames/light. He'll see it in his terms, pouring your Ki into an object, but he won't assume he knows how to use the object or that it will work for him.<br /> <br /> If Wonders are &quot;if you believe in this it will always work&quot;, then that's a slightly un-nuanced approach. Surely it would make more sense within the wider scope of Paradigms and the Mage Lore if Wonders only worked if you believe that they will work for you? Why does the non-sleeper who uses a wand suddenly think that a set of magical wings will work for him on the first try? They can doubt that they can use them and still not be a sleeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Storytellers Companion pp.65<br /> &quot;<b>Sleepers and the Tools of Wonder </b><br /> While most Sleepers cannot recharge Talismans, they can make use of them, as long as they both believe in the paradigm of the mage who created the item and they Resonate strongly with the maker's personality. Depending on the Talisman, Paradox might also apply to the Sleeper who uses it - one of the most classic Paradoxes being loss of the Talisman. Talismans will not work for those who do not accept their paradigm. However, mages are strong-willed enough that they may override the Nature and Demeanor of any Talisman except in the case of an extraordinarily powerful magic object and an unusually weak-willed mage.<br /> <br /> Charms and Gadgets will work for anyone who accepts the paradigm under which they were made, or is in the area where that paradigm holds sway (even if that person doesn't know that the object is in fact magical). For example, if Kate, who lives in the Irish countryside and believes in witchrat, faeries and all the rest, were to put on some flying salve, thinking it was just hand creme, she'd find herself airborne whether she wanted to or not. Her cousin from Dublin wouldn't have any such troubles, unless he came out to the country and was far away from citified things. Paradox might also apply were Kate to use that Charm in a vulgar Fashion- like going to New York and flying over the Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade - but since such a thing might be explained as some kind of high-tech advertising stunt, this penalty applies at Storyteller discretion. Fire-time uses and accidents should be treated as static magic, but flying through the air is Paradoxical enough for most Sleepers.&quot;<br /> <br /> So unless you want to claim that Sorcerers are like Mages, then they can't use the objects unless they believe in the paradigm, and if they don't believe in the paradigm, they are effectively sleepers.<br /> <br /> To decide sorcerers are &quot;near enough&quot; to mages to not count as witnesses would imply that static magic and awakened magic are more alike than any source indicates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:05:32-08:00","id":1045762,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a> The rules outright state that Sorcerers and other Night-Folk aren't Sleepers. They don't clarify (to the best of my knowledge) whether Night-Folk can use Wonders. So the real question is &quot;can Night-Folk use Wonders?&quot; I'd say yes for Sorcerers and other living creatures, but only if the Sorcerer's paradigm matches that of the Wonder within a certain degree of latency. Sorcerers are a special exception and can't be considered the same as humans when figuring out whether they're sleepers or not; like I say they are very very very rarely Sleepers, as confirmed by both Mage 20th and Sorcerer Revised, so you need to come up with a Wonders system that works with that by yourself. I've given one which works and makes sense, even if there isn't text backing it up.<br /> <br /> As for Vampires and the like... I'm less sure. Saying yes would be simplest, but there's also some poetic justice to Dead Creatures being unable to use Wonders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:07:20-08:00","id":1045764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1045745#post1045745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you allow Flaws? Why do you feel a need to balance characters who intentionally choose to play someone with a limp or mental illness?<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't consider choosing sorcerer over mage to be a flaw. Everyone else is fundamentally a mage in a mage game, no matter their difference in flaws, paradigm, etc. A limping mage and a non-limping mage are still both mages. It'd be like if everyone else is driving mint 2016 Ferrari Aperta's in a race and the one guy wants to drive a 2000 Buick LeSabre with 200,000 miles, I don't feel the need to put extra effort to make sure that Buick is equally effective just because that's what he wants. Even more specifically for this example, you can take flaws to be lesser generation in Vampire. But you are still fundamentally a Vampire. Whereas this is a case of choosing to play something (a sorcerer) that is fundamentally different and worse than what the Mages are, even with it being an existing thing within the splat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The implication that wanting mechanical recompense for playing as a mini-Splat somehow goes against RP or organic characters is The Stormwind Fallacy, however. </div> </div> </div> Not the intended implication. Merely that 'I'm playing an almost objectively worse mini-splat, I deserve mechanical benefits to make me equivalent to something better than me' is asking for unnecessary special treatment. There has to be a limit. If a player said, 'I want to play a normal mortal human' in a mage game, I don't feel the need to give them special treatment for doing something different. I don't fault them for wanting to play the character they want and be the equivalent of other characters/effective. I also don't think ever player desire deserves to be indulged. Wanting to play something special and wanting special treatment is too much imo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree that Ghouls and Kinfolk can be fun with no balancing whatsoever, and I've seen them both work well. However, those are differences of degrees, not kind. The Kinfolk have weaker gifts and a single form, the Ghouls have weaker Disciplines and a lesser status. Mages, on the other hand, are not just Sorcerers who start with higher levels in Paths, they don't use Paths at all. </div> </div> </div> Sure, but you'll still need to give a fair amount of extra benefits to the person to playing the ghoul of kinfolk to make them the equivalent in effectiveness as to a vampire or werewolf. I think the point remains that if you are playing something fundamentally different in game terms, you don't necessarily deserve special treatment. But as usual, it centers back to my wish that there was an X20 sorcerer book that inherently made Paths more competitive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now playing a Sorcerer with no balancing whatsoever certainly could be fun, however if an ST decided that they did want to balance it, what would you recommend? That was basically my initial request, ideas on balancing the two types of Starting Character at least a little bit. </div> </div> </div> I was mostly addressing the questions of 'would you allow it and how would you run it.' But if I was allowing it, and if I felt the need to give compensation, I'd go with XP compensation. There really is no easy way that I see to match paths with the sheer versatility of spheres without just giving them more to work with. But the easiest way would be that. I'd have to fiddle with the numbers and expected Chronicle length to settle on a number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:22:25-08:00","id":1045771,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12552_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12552\" data-vbnamecard=\"12552\">Monalfie</a> RE Ghouls, it can be done. Just make the Ghoul antique and play the strangeness of the Prince's (or Bishop's) 150 year Ghoul. Obviously the Prince is very keen to make sure that this Coterie of misfits doesn't screw up, so he sends along his trusted servant to keep an eye on these Neonates. The Ghoul has 1 dot in a few Disciplines and great Attributes/Abilities, but little scope for growth or development in the Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, with Kinfolk, the best solution is to make them a Sorcerer. It's an established bit of lore that Kinfolk produce Sorcerers, and that Garou (and Fera) are very protective of Sorcerous Kinfolk. This is assuming your ST is capable of keeping two systems in their head (most experienced STs can handle multiple systems from what I've seen).<br /> <br /> And I think it's a bit harsh to describe this as &quot;asking for special treatment to make me equivalent to something better than me&quot;. In reality it's going to be &quot;I really love the Sorcery system and have a great idea for a Sorcerer who chooses not to Awaken for personal reasons, however I don't want to be a ragdoll or dead weight in the chronicle, or rely on the Spheres of others to buff me, so can I start with a few more Path/Ritual dots and more EXP please?&quot; I feel like there's a bad feeling here, where you're assuming that this Sorcerer PC has dark intentions and is trying to trick something out of you. Like everyone else, they're just here to have fun. If they were trying to game the system or power-game, they'd have a faithful paradigm with True Faith in some entity whose rules/teachings line up with &quot;what I wanted to do anyways&quot;, gaining a paradigm to do whatever they want with &quot;I pray for X&quot; as a catch-all, and all of the (many) benefits of True Faith. That's the sort of thing STs should be skeptical of and give negative responses to, not &quot;am Sorcerer, plz buff so I can haz fun?&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:26:59-08:00","id":1045774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1045762#post1045762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a> Sorcerers are a special exception and can't be considered the same as humans when figuring out whether they're sleepers or not; like I say they are very very very rarely Sleepers, as confirmed by both Mage 20th and Sorcerer Revised, so you need to come up with a Wonders system that works with that by yourself. I've given one which works and makes sense, even if there isn't text backing it up..</div> </div> </div> </div>Source please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:30:33-08:00","id":1045776,"title":"","content":"Easiest way to balance is to just encourage the Sorcerer player to build around a primary Path, and start it at 4 or 5. (Not extra, just don't push a cap on starting Paths.) It may only be one, good, strong effect, but chances of a starting Mage being able to pull that same thing off are slim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:32:56-08:00","id":1045779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1045774#post1045774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Source please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure about M20, but SRev merit everyone mentioned is called Style Sleeper. Basically they believe their own Paradigm, but nobody else's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:36:41-08:00","id":1045783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1045779#post1045779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure about M20, but SRev merit everyone mentioned is called Style Sleeper. Basically they believe their own Paradigm, but nobody else's.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a> And if you search the term &quot;Night-Folk&quot; in your M20 PDF you'll get a bit talking about disbelief and supernatural creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:52:46-08:00","id":1045794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1045776#post1045776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Easiest way to balance is to just encourage the Sorcerer player to build around a primary Path, and start it at 4 or 5. (Not extra, just don't push a cap on starting Paths.) It may only be one, good, strong effect, but chances of a starting Mage being able to pull that same thing off are slim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, you could treat them normally, do Equal For All character generation, but then just give the Sorcerer a kinder EXP track. So rather than Paths being Current Rating x (can't remember the exact number), make it 1 or 2 lower. True Magick gets exponentially stronger as the characters level up, they go from having incredible senses of the world around them to altering it in incredible ways (in a small area) in about half a Story... so just give the Sorcerer a steeper Line so that the Exponential curve of Magickal progression doesn't obliterate it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:57:00-08:00","id":1045799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1045771#post1045771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12552_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12552\" data-vbnamecard=\"12552\">Monalfie</a> RE Ghouls, it can be done. Just make the Ghoul antique and play the strangeness of the Prince's (or Bishop's) 150 year Ghoul. Obviously the Prince is very keen to make sure that this Coterie of misfits doesn't screw up, so he sends along his trusted servant to keep an eye on these Neonates. The Ghoul has 1 dot in a few Disciplines and great Attributes/Abilities, but little scope for growth or development in the Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, with Kinfolk, the best solution is to make them a Sorcerer. It's an established bit of lore that Kinfolk produce Sorcerers, and that Garou (and Fera) are very protective of Sorcerous Kinfolk. This is assuming your ST is capable of keeping two systems in their head (most experienced STs can handle multiple systems from what I've seen).</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure. I'm not saying it can't necessarily be done. Just that it will necessarily involve giving that player special consideration if system balance is the end goal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I think it's a bit harsh to describe this as &quot;asking for special treatment to make me equivalent to something better than me&quot;. In reality it's going to be &quot;I really love the Sorcery system and have a great idea for a Sorcerer who chooses not to Awaken for personal reasons, however I don't want to be a ragdoll or dead weight in the chronicle, or rely on the Spheres of others to buff me, so can I start with a few more Path/Ritual dots and more EXP please?&quot; </div> </div> </div> Again, I don't have issue if someone wants that. I just also think there should be a limit on how much wanting to play something else should be indulged, in the same way if they wanted to play a vampire, ghoul, kinfolk, normal human, hunter, etc. in a mage game. Or even, again, a ghoul in a vampire game as well. I think there becomes a point where special consideration because more trouble than it is worth. I'm not even inherently against some special treatment for the sake of balance, but I personally think there is also special difficulty in any Mages with non-Mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like there's a bad feeling here, where you're assuming that this Sorcerer PC has dark intentions and is trying to trick something out of you. Like everyone else, they're just here to have fun. If they were trying to game the system or power-game, they'd have a faithful paradigm with True Faith in some entity whose rules/teachings line up with &quot;what I wanted to do anyways&quot;, gaining a paradigm to do whatever they want with &quot;I pray for X&quot; as a catch-all, and all of the (many) benefits of True Faith. That's the sort of thing STs should be skeptical of and give negative responses to, not &quot;am Sorcerer, plz buff so I can haz fun?&quot;. </div> </div> </div> Not about dark intentions. As I said, I'm just skeptical of why in a Mage game, where people are playing Mages, someone is choosing to play something that is Not a Mage, and special balance consideration should be made for them. If they can't have fun with a sorcerer in an explicit mage centered game without special treatment, I'd suggest not choosing to play a sorcerer. Even further, if they can't have fun playing a mage in a mage game, I'd suggest not playing in a mage game. Maybe that sounds harsh, but if there is a fundamental difference about what the players want to play, I'd suggest having a discussion about what game they want to do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T09:16:00-08:00","id":1045812,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12552_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12552\" data-vbnamecard=\"12552\">Monalfie</a> I think there is something to be said for the specific dynamic of being a Sorcerer in a Mage game. M20 decided to drop the Sorcerers are common in the Traditions etc. thing because they didn't have enough space to do it justice (there's a sidebar on it) however I do personally love the interactions between Sorcery and Magick and think that it should be a bigger theme in Mage. So it isn't as random as turning up to a Mage game and asking to play a Vampire, or turning up and saying &quot;can we play Sorcerer&quot;, it's a person asking if they can play a Sorcerer in a Mage game, because they want the very specific dynamic that engenders. And since the systems are difficult to compare, I think it's fair for there to be some form of balancing factor, and it doesn't even need to be a complex one.<br /> <br /> So if we can agree that there is value in playing a Sorcerer among Mages, which is an interesting concept (at least to some people) and could be fun to explore, it might be worth talking about ways to make them mechanically relevant. Party Balance is a big deal, and that's why you have a Session 0. If everyone turns up with Prime, Life and Matter, and no one has Spirit or Correspondence, your Party has hit a brick wall already. Character Generation must have a collaborative element to it if you're going to get a group of Characters who can all take turns in the spotlight and come from different walks of life. It's just more interesting if they're different and are good at different things. So if there is to be any collaboration (in Vampire this is less of a problem since collaboration isn't the default) you need to consider this party balance, where everyone brings something &quot;to the table&quot; so-to-speak. If Julien and Clara are both Life experts who are faithful and focused on Healing, perhaps nudge one of them away from that concept to pick something else they'd like to play, being sensitive and avoiding pissing either of them off.<br /> <br /> So, how does our Sorcerer factor into this? Say they run a normal character gen and have Conveyance 5 and nothing else. They're now a Car, Teleporting Device, Horse or whatever you want to call them. Okay, this time they've got Hellfire 3 and Conjuration 2. They're now something akin to Forces 2 and Correspondence 2, except they don't have 2 extra Path dots left, and they can't do the trillion other things you can do with those two spheres. Say you gave them 1 dot in Alchemy, Hellfire, Mana Manipulation, Summoning/Binding/Warding and Healing. They can now mix up Aspirin, light cigarettes and zap bugs, sense &quot;supernaturals&quot; with no real idea of what they are or how powerful they are, summon animals and make them obey and get rid of a nasty cold. No matter how you mix it, they will always be... kind of superfluous to the Party after character generation. And if no one is, say, a Healer, you'll end up with a considerably weaker Healer than if you had a Mage do it, since Life 3 and Entropy 3 is a far better Healer than Path of Healing 5. So now the question is just: &quot;why did The Higher-ups give us THIS GUY instead of another Mage?&quot; 'Wants to be useful to the Party' shouldn't be contraversial, and I run a very inclusive table, so I personally feel the best solution is to give them more dots. Make it 10 dots. Okay, now we can start with Conveyance 5 and Hellfire 5. Now we have a guy who is VERY mobile and can carry the party places, and is also some safe paradox-free fire support. Conjuration 5 and Alchemy 5. Now we have a guy who has a mixture for every occasion sitting in the fridge back home, ready to be pulled out of his coat pocket to help when they're needed. As a result, we now have a good reason for why they are there, how they are going to contribute to 'the team', and that allows you to carry out the unique RP opportunity of being a Sorcerer assisting a group of Mages on some quest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-08-2017, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T10:49:16-08:00","id":1045860,"title":"","content":"I generally think that two Sorcerers are worth one Mage (if you are using 'Equality for All' rules). Sorcerers are fine beginning characters, but they get left behind by Mages in mixed games pretty quickly (strangely enough, they retain their utility longer in non-Mage games much longer because they bring capabilities that are difficult for other supernatural creatures to duplicate). Of course, Sorcerers retain their defensive superiority over Mages forever, so Sorcerers are useful as counterspell specialists against enemy Mages (each counterspell optimized Sorcerer can shut down two enemy Mages by splitting their counterspell dice pools).<br /> <br /> Sorcerers are probably best as NPCs in Mage games, and they make interesting threats against PC Mages when they are created under 'Equality for All' rules. The Union probably makes good use of its Extraordinary Citizens because they can be sent to deal with Reality Deviants without requiring much Enlightened Member support. Its Enlightened Members can be used for greater concerns while its Extraordinary Citizens deal with lesser concerns.<br /> <br /> For example, a ten-person squad that consisted of Extraordinary Citizens working for the Union would be a problem for five Tradition Mages because five of the Extraordinary Citizens could shut down the magic of the five Tradition Mages with counterspells while the other five would be able to capture the five Tradition Mages. If they are prepared for trouble, the five extraordinary Citizens who are not tasked to counterspell duty could have hung spells that could do massive amounts of damage (Conjuration 5 could be prepared ahead of time to bring twenty HMMVVs with four soldiers each from within 5 miles of the target, Fascination 5 could be prepared ahead of time to force a group of Mages to surrender, Fortune 5 could be prepared ahead of time to death curse a group of Mages, Hellfire 5 could be prepared ahead of time to summon lightning that deals 8 dice of aggravated damage to everyone within a 20 square foot area, Shapeshifting 5 could be prepared ahead of time to turn two enemy Mages into sloths for a scene, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T12:41:35-08:00","id":1045916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1045860#post1045860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally think that two Sorcerers are worth one Mage (if you are using 'Equality for All' rules). Sorcerers are fine beginning characters, but they get left behind by Mages in mixed games pretty quickly (strangely enough, they retain their utility longer in non-Mage games much longer because they bring capabilities that are difficult for other supernatural creatures to duplicate). Of course, Sorcerers retain their defensive superiority over Mages forever, so Sorcerers are useful as counterspell specialists against enemy Mages (each counterspell optimized Sorcerer can shut down two enemy Mages by splitting their counterspell dice pools).<br /> <br /> Sorcerers are probably best as NPCs in Mage games, and they make interesting threats against PC Mages when they are created under 'Equality for All' rules. The Union probably makes good use of its Extraordinary Citizens because they can be sent to deal with Reality Deviants without requiring much Enlightened Member support. Its Enlightened Members can be used for greater concerns while its Extraordinary Citizens deal with lesser concerns.<br /> <br /> For example, a ten-person squad that consisted of Extraordinary Citizens working for the Union would be a problem for five Tradition Mages because five of the Extraordinary Citizens could shut down the magic of the five Tradition Mages with counterspells while the other five would be able to capture the five Tradition Mages. If they are prepared for trouble, the five extraordinary Citizens who are not tasked to counterspell duty could have hung spells that could do massive amounts of damage (Conjuration 5 could be prepared ahead of time to bring twenty HMMVVs with four soldiers each from within 5 miles of the target, Fascination 5 could be prepared ahead of time to force a group of Mages to surrender, Fortune 5 could be prepared ahead of time to death curse a group of Mages, Hellfire 5 could be prepared ahead of time to summon lightning that deals 8 dice of aggravated damage to everyone within a 20 square foot area, Shapeshifting 5 could be prepared ahead of time to turn two enemy Mages into sloths for a scene, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like this, but remember that the Technocracy's Sorcerers can NEVER become Reality Deviants. If they are using Fascination 5, there had better be a good explanation (forcing a hypnotic state using a flashing light as a focus), same with all of the others. Mystic Sorcerers are much more free in that they don't need to worry about that sort of thing, they can just conjure fire rather than needing a flamethrower (or similar) as a focus, but the Technosorcerer has the edge of conforming with people's expectations, it's easier to make people believe in it and avoid drawing attention from malevolent forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T14:45:17-08:00","id":1046007,"title":"","content":"Of course, Extraordinary Citizens do not depend on outdated mysticism. 'Countermagic' is created by focused subsonic disruption fields that break the concentration of Reality Deviants while 'Fascination' is just the activation of common memes spread by Advanced Memetic Engineering. There is nothing mystical involved, just move along and ignore the sloths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T15:34:15-08:00","id":1046033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1046007#post1046007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, Extraordinary Citizens do not depend on outdated mysticism. 'Countermagic' is created by focused subsonic disruption fields that break the concentration of Reality Deviants while 'Fascination' is just the activation of common memes spread by Advanced Memetic Engineering. There is nothing mystical involved, just move along and ignore the sloths.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Naturally, these sonic disruptions cause Genetic Degradation at an alarming rate. These Reality Deviants are highly unstable due to their unnatural arts, and so they typically devolve into primates when exposed to these disruptions.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:14:34-08:00","id":1046046,"title":"","content":"Sloths aren't primates, their closest relatives are anteaters, so you may be thinking of lemurs. I think a more adequate explanation would be 'The Neural Inhibitor gases produce shared hallucinations that affect anyone who gets even a trace of the gas, though it primarily makes its target(s) believe that they temporarily transformed into a specific animal and, as a side effect, witnesses that receive trace exposure believe that the target(s) have become that specific animal'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T03:42:37-08:00","id":1046235,"title":"","content":"Eh, I struggle to see someone who has Shapeshifting 5 and has no clue what they're doing. I think they need to know that they're actually changing their shape. Just say the gas is a hyper-mutagen which forces a specific form but retains a specific mass, so a technosorcerer can't make you into a cat since they don't think they can delete mass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T06:19:03-08:00","id":1046277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1045709-playing-a-sorcerer-in-a-mage-chronicle?p=1046235#post1046235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I struggle to see someone who has Shapeshifting 5 and has no clue what they're doing. I think they need to know that they're actually changing their shape. Just say the gas is a hyper-mutagen which forces a specific form but retains a specific mass, so a technosorcerer can't make you into a cat since they don't think they can delete mass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Variation of cloning and consciousness transplants? Have to get back to recover biomass from the vat or risk getting stuck?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":